module densityDetection
module viabilityDetection
module transformationQC

manifest E_coli
manifest S_cerevisiae
manifest C_cryptica
manifest LB_Broth
manifest YPD_Broth
manifest F2_Media
manifest EthidiumHomodimer1
manifest TritonX100
manifest pTriEx_YFP_Plasmid
manifest CaCl2_Solution

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Integrated Microbioreactor for Culture and Analysis of
// Bacteria, Algae and Yeast ("BAY" microbioreactor).
// Au, Shih, Wheeler - Biomed Microdevices (2011) 13:41-50
// DOI: 10.1007/s10544-010-9469-3
//
// Protocol: automated digital-microfluidic (DMF) culture of
// three microorganism types (E. coli, S. cerevisiae,
// C. cryptica) in a ~70 uL "mother drop", with periodic
// semi-continuous circular-path mixing, absorbance-based
// density monitoring, an on-chip fluorescent viability assay
// (EthD-1 +/- Triton X-100) for yeast, and on-chip genetic
// transformation of E. coli with a YFP reporter plasmid.
//
// NOTE ON DAUGHTER-DROPLET ABSTRACTION: The paper dispenses
// ~7 uL daughter droplets from the ~70 uL mother drop for
// absorbance measurement, then returns them to the mother
// drop afterward (Section 2.5, Fig. 2b). lilott8/BioScript
// does not reliably support split/re-merge of a single mother
// droplet without stranding fragments (see array/split
// limitations noted in reference protocols). Absorbance
// detection is therefore modelled directly on the culture
// droplet itself (non-consumptive `detect`), which is
// functionally equivalent to the daughter-droplet round trip
// for CFG purposes.
//
// NOTE ON MIXING/INCUBATION ABSTRACTION: Semi-continuous
// circular-path mixing (Fig. 2a, ~1.5 s actuation per cycle,
// repeated at Table 1 intervals) is modelled as a single
// short `mix` step (inoculation) followed by a `heat` step
// at the culture temperature for the duration of one
// absorbance-measurement interval (Table 1: bacteria 1 h,
// yeast 2 h, algae 24 h), representing one representative
// growth/measurement cycle rather than the full multi-day
// unrolled loop (BioScript has no loop construct).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main            -- entry: bacteria culture + density check
//   BB2  bactPass         -- bactGrowthSignal > 0: culture continues
//   BB3  bactFail         -- bactGrowthSignal <= 0: contamination, drain
//   BB4  bactJoin         -- join: yeast culture arm begins
//   BB5  yeastPass        -- yeastGrowthSignal > 0: culture continues
//   BB6  yeastFail        -- yeastGrowthSignal <= 0: contamination, drain
//   BB7  yeastJoin        -- join: algae culture arm begins
//   BB8  algaePass        -- algaeGrowthSignal > 0: culture continues
//   BB9  algaeFail        -- algaeGrowthSignal <= 0: contamination, drain
//   BB10 algaeJoin        -- join: yeast viability assay begins
//   BB11 viabilityPass    -- viabilitySignal > 0: viable cells, dispose
//   BB12 viabilityFail    -- viabilitySignal <= 0: non-viable, drain
//   BB13 viabilityJoin    -- join: E. coli transformation begins
//   BB14 transformPass    -- transformSignal > 0: colonies formed, dispose
//   BB15 transformFail    -- transformSignal <= 0: no colonies, drain
//   BB16 finalCleanup     -- terminal: dispose transformation QC signal
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// BACTERIA ARM (Section 2.2/2.5, Table 1): E. coli DH5alpha
//   grown in LB broth at 37 C. Mother drop mixed in a circular
//   pattern every 2.5 min; absorbance (600 nm) measured every
//   1 h and used as the growth/contamination QC signal.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

motherDropBact  = dispense 1 units of E_coli
lbMedia         = dispense 1 units of LB_Broth
bactCulture     = mix motherDropBact with lbMedia for 5s

// Represents one 1-h inter-measurement incubation interval
// (Table 1: absorbance measurement frequency, bacteria = 1 h)
// under semi-continuous circular mixing at 37 C.
heat bactCulture at 37c for 60m

bactGrowthSignal = detect densityDetection on bactCulture for 1s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Bacteria growth QC gate
// Pass (BB2): bactGrowthSignal > 0 -> absorbance increasing,
//             culture proceeding normally; dispose (continue
//             represented by disposal of this cycle's droplet).
// Fail (BB3): bactGrowthSignal <= 0 -> no growth/contamination;
//             drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (bactJoin).
// ============================================================

if (bactGrowthSignal > 0) {
    dispose bactCulture
} else {
    drain bactCulture
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: bactJoin
// Dispose bacteria growth QC signal. Control falls into the
// yeast culture arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose bactGrowthSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// YEAST ARM (Section 2.2/2.5, Table 1): S. cerevisiae BY4741
//   grown in YPD broth at 30 C. Mother drop mixed every
//   2.5 min; absorbance (600 nm) measured every 2 h.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

motherDropYeast   = dispense 1 units of S_cerevisiae
ypdMedia          = dispense 1 units of YPD_Broth
yeastCulture      = mix motherDropYeast with ypdMedia for 5s

// Represents one 2-h inter-measurement incubation interval
// (Table 1: absorbance measurement frequency, yeast = 2 h).
heat yeastCulture at 30c for 120m

yeastGrowthSignal = detect densityDetection on yeastCulture for 1s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Yeast growth QC gate
// Pass (BB5): yeastGrowthSignal > 0 -> culture proceeding
//             normally; dispose.
// Fail (BB6): yeastGrowthSignal <= 0 -> no growth/contamination;
//             drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (yeastJoin).
// ============================================================

if (yeastGrowthSignal > 0) {
    dispose yeastCulture
} else {
    drain yeastCulture
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: yeastJoin
// Dispose yeast growth QC signal. Control falls into the
// algae culture arm (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose yeastGrowthSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ALGAE ARM (Section 2.2/2.5, Table 1): C. cryptica grown in
//   f/2 medium (+ biotin/cyanocobalamin) at 14 C under
//   continuous illumination. Mother drop mixed every 120 min;
//   absorbance (660 nm) measured every 24 h.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

motherDropAlgae   = dispense 1 units of C_cryptica
f2Media           = dispense 1 units of F2_Media
algaeCulture      = mix motherDropAlgae with f2Media for 5s

// Represents one 24-h inter-measurement incubation interval
// (Table 1: absorbance measurement frequency, algae = 24 h).
heat algaeCulture at 14c for 1440m

algaeGrowthSignal = detect densityDetection on algaeCulture for 1s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Algae growth QC gate
// Pass (BB8): algaeGrowthSignal > 0 -> culture proceeding
//             normally; dispose.
// Fail (BB9): algaeGrowthSignal <= 0 -> no growth/contamination;
//             drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (algaeJoin).
// ============================================================

if (algaeGrowthSignal > 0) {
    dispose algaeCulture
} else {
    drain algaeCulture
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: algaeJoin
// Dispose algae growth QC signal. Control falls into the
// yeast viability assay branch (BB11/BB12).
// ============================================================

dispose algaeGrowthSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// VIABILITY ASSAY (Section 2.7): S. cerevisiae grown 4 h at
//   30 C with automated mixing, then merged with a dispensed
//   droplet containing 2 uM Ethidium homodimer-1 (EthD-1) and,
//   for the lytic-control condition, 0.05% (v/v) Triton X-100.
//   Combined droplet mixed along the linear path (~10
//   actuations), incubated 30 C for 1 h, and read out by
//   fluorescence (EthD-1 stains dead/compromised cells).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

yeastForAssay   = dispense 1 units of S_cerevisiae
ypdMedia2       = dispense 1 units of YPD_Broth
assayCulture    = mix yeastForAssay with ypdMedia2 for 5s

// 4-h pre-assay incubation at 30 C with automated mixing.
heat assayCulture at 30c for 240m

ethd1Dye        = dispense 1 units of EthidiumHomodimer1
tritonReagent   = dispense 1 units of TritonX100
dyeTritonMix    = mix ethd1Dye with tritonReagent for 5s

// Merge and mix along the linear path (~10 actuations).
stainedYeast    = mix assayCulture with dyeTritonMix for 10s

// Incubation at 30 C for 1 h prior to fluorescence readout.
heat stainedYeast at 30c for 60m

viabilitySignal = detect viabilityDetection on stainedYeast for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: Viability QC gate
// Pass (BB11): viabilitySignal > 0 -> viable cell population
//              detected; dispose.
// Fail (BB12): viabilitySignal <= 0 -> non-viable/compromised
//              population (e.g. Triton X-100 lytic condition,
//              >99% non-viable per Fig. 5); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB13 (viabilityJoin).
// ============================================================

if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedYeast
} else {
    drain stainedYeast
}

// ============================================================
// BB13: viabilityJoin
// Dispose viability QC signal. Control falls into the E. coli
// transformation branch (BB14/BB15).
// ============================================================

dispose viabilitySignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// TRANSFORMATION (Section 2.8): E. coli (without ampicillin
//   resistance) grown 1 h at 37 C to early/mid-log phase, then
//   chilled on ice 5 min. A droplet of pTriEx-YFP plasmid DNA
//   (200 ng) in 0.20 M CaCl2 is merged with the culture droplet
//   and mixed (~10 actuations). The combined droplet is chilled
//   on ice 1 h, heat-shocked at 42 C for 50 s, cooled on ice for
//   1 min, then incubated at 37 C for 1 h with automated mixing
//   before being spread on an ampicillin LB agar plate
//   (off-chip) to confirm successful transformation (Fig. 5d).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

competentEcoli  = dispense 1 units of E_coli
lbMedia3        = dispense 1 units of LB_Broth
transformCulture = mix competentEcoli with lbMedia3 for 5s

// 1-h growth to early/mid-log phase at 37 C with mixing.
heat transformCulture at 37c for 60m

// Pre-chill on ice for 5 min prior to plasmid addition.
heat transformCulture at 4c for 300s

plasmidDrop      = dispense 1 units of pTriEx_YFP_Plasmid
cacl2Drop        = dispense 1 units of CaCl2_Solution
plasmidCacl2Mix  = mix plasmidDrop with cacl2Drop for 5s

// Merge culture with plasmid/CaCl2 droplet, mixed along the
// sample region path (~10 actuations).
transformMix     = mix transformCulture with plasmidCacl2Mix for 10s

// Chill on ice for 1 h.
heat transformMix at 4c for 60m

// Heat shock: 42 C for 50 s.
heat transformMix at 42c for 50s

// Cool on ice for an additional 1 min.
heat transformMix at 4c for 60s

// Recovery incubation: 37 C for 1 h with automated mixing.
heat transformMix at 37c for 60m

// Off-chip readout: droplet spread on ampicillin LB agar plate
// and incubated overnight at 37 C; transformationQC abstracts
// the resulting colony-formation observation (Fig. 5d).
transformSignal  = detect transformationQC on transformMix for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB14 / BB15: Transformation QC gate
// Pass (BB14): transformSignal > 0 -> ampicillin-resistant,
//              YFP-expressing colonies observed; dispose.
// Fail (BB15): transformSignal <= 0 -> no colonies (failed
//              transformation); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB16 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (transformSignal > 0) {
    dispose transformMix
} else {
    drain transformMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB16: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose transformation QC signal droplet; experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose transformSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
